# Local development. Copy this file to .env (gitignored).
# The app loads .env on startup and leaves variables that are already
# set in the environment alone. Production sets those directly and
# does not need this file.
#
# Cursor worktree setup copies .env into a new worktree only when that
# checkout has no .env yet and the file contains safe local settings.
# It does not copy production credentials, real SMTP hosts, or
# SMTP_ALLOW_REAL. Named agent servers set ADDR, PORT, DB_PATH, and
# BASE_URL themselves, and they force console mail. A .env file or an
# inherited shell cannot switch an agent server to SMTP.
#
# Mail defaults to the console. Login and verification links are written
# to that process's log. Missing mail settings do not fall back to SMTP.
#
# Local MailHog, when you want it: SMTP on 1025, web inbox at
# http://localhost:8025. Uncomment the two lines below. This is local
# mail, not a real delivery.
# SMTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# SMTP_PORT=1025
#
# Real SMTP from development needs all of: a non-local SMTP_HOST,
# SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, and SMTP_ALLOW_REAL=1. Credentials alone do not
# send. Production does not read SMTP_ALLOW_REAL; it uses SMTP_HOST.
# SMTP_ALLOW_REAL=
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# MAIL_FROM=Track Anything <hello@trackanything.io>
#
# MAIL_BACKEND is a development choice: console, local, or smtp.
# Leave it unset to derive the backend from SMTP_HOST. Named agent
# servers set MAIL_BACKEND=console.
# MAIL_BACKEND=

# Other settings, and the defaults used when they are unset:
# ADDR=:8080
# DB_PATH=data/trackanything.db
# ENV=dev
# BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
# Production sets TRUSTED_IP_HEADER=Fly-Client-IP because Fly Proxy is the
# trusted public ingress. Leave it unset in development. The app then uses
# the connection address and ignores Fly-Client-IP, CF-Connecting-IP, and
# X-Forwarded-For.
# TRUSTED_IP_HEADER=
# Production requires TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY and TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY.
# Leave both unset in development. The app then uses Cloudflare's
# always-pass test keys. Do not put production keys in this file.
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
